/**
 * @file engine/tilemap/tilemap
 *
 * Complete tilemap facade: `import engine.tilemap` brings in the lattices, the
 * storage, the tileset, the ECS tiles, collision, loading and drawing.
 *
 * ## What this package is
 *
 * A tilemap is a lattice, a stack of dense layers on it, and a tileset the
 * layers draw from. Square, isometric (diamond and staggered) and hexagonal
 * lattices are all supported, in every coordinate system a tile editor exports,
 * and everything above `engine.tilemap.coords` is written against the geometry
 * rather than against a particular lattice — so a map changes shape by changing
 * one field.
 *
 * ## A map in six lines
 *
 * ```azora
 * import engine.tilemap
 *
 * var tiles = tileSetFromAtlas("terrain",
 *     tileAtlasLoadOrEmpty(app, "assets/terrain.bmp", 16, 16))
 * tiles.addTraitsRange(0, 15, traitSolid)
 *
 * var level = tilemapSquare("level", 64, 64, 16.0, 16.0, tiles)
 * layerFill(level.layers[0], 3)
 *
 * fin camera = cameraForApp(app, Vec2(512.0, 512.0), 2.0)
 * drawTilemap(app, level, camera, app.timeNow())
 * ```
 *
 * ## Where things live
 *
 * - `engine.tilemap.types` — coordinates, sizes, colours, flags, faults
 * - `engine.tilemap.hex` — hex algebra: axial, cube and the four offset systems
 * - `engine.tilemap.coords` — the geometry: tile to world, world to tile, culling
 * - `engine.tilemap.storage` — dense layers and the cell-to-entity index
 * - `engine.tilemap.atlas` — tile sheets and multi-sheet index spaces
 * - `engine.tilemap.anim` — animated tiles, resolved from the clock
 * - `engine.tilemap.tileset` — artwork plus per-tile traits
 * - `engine.tilemap.map` — the map: geometry, layers, tileset
 * - `engine.tilemap.neighbor` — who touches whom, on any lattice
 * - `engine.tilemap.collide` — overlap, swept movement and rays, on `engine.physics.d2`
 * - `engine.tilemap.load` — comma-separated and packed binary layers
 * - `engine.tilemap.draw` — the camera and the renderer
 * - `engine.tilemap.ecs` — per-tile entities and the systems that sync them
 *
 * ## Failure
 *
 * Anything that can be refused returns `T ?! TilemapFault`: an off-map write, a
 * malformed level file, a tile index the tileset does not contain. Propagate it
 * with `try`, handle it with `try { … } catch { … }`, or take a default with
 * `expr catch fallback`.
 *
 * Results with more than one *valid* answer stay tagged unions, because they are
 * not failures: [TileLookup] distinguishes an empty cell from an off-map one,
 * and [TilePick], [TileEntity], [AtlasPick] and [TileRayHit] read the same way.
 *
 * @since 0.0.4
 */
module engine.tilemap

exposed import engine.tilemap.types
exposed import engine.tilemap.hex
exposed import engine.tilemap.coords
exposed import engine.tilemap.storage
exposed import engine.tilemap.atlas
exposed import engine.tilemap.anim
exposed import engine.tilemap.tileset
exposed import engine.tilemap.map
exposed import engine.tilemap.neighbor
exposed import engine.tilemap.collide
exposed import engine.tilemap.load
exposed import engine.tilemap.draw
exposed import engine.tilemap.ecs
